 "notes": "Turlough O'Carolan wrote this planxty (a tune in honour of a patron) for Colonel John Irwin in the early 1700s. Play it as a lilting waltz, three beats to the bar, not too fast. Part B is higher and brighter; the cuts on its repeated notes give it a little lift.",
